steamclient64.dll and steam.exe for running Steam games with
proton-openbsd, without Valve's Steam client.

Most games use the Steamworks API (steam_api64.dll), which needs a
running Steam client and its steamclient64.dll.  This package provides
an open implementation of the client interfaces: it reports the account
proton-launcher logged in with (SteamID, persona name, owned apps and
DLC), keeps user stats, achievements and Steam Cloud files in a local
directory, and delivers callbacks and asynchronous call results.
Online services (lobbies, peer-to-peer networking, workshop,
leaderboards) report failure, as Steam does when it is offline.
It does not remove DRM; games protected with Steam's DRM wrapper still
need Valve's client.

proton-openbsd installs the files into each prefix and runs games that
have SteamAppId set (proton-launcher sets it) under steam.exe.
